{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/31765-lingering-bite-on-the-undead","id":31765,"title":"Lingering Bite on the Undead","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-17T10:34:29-08:00","id":31765,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Lingering Bite on the Undead","content":"Sorry, I wasn't sure where to put this. I was just wondering about a rules discussion on what happens if a Werewolf used Lingering Bite as per The Pure pg 115 on something without a natural healing rate such as a vampire. The wording says it can't be healed by supernatural means, lays out standard healing rates for the injury, and then says that the Rite of Healing would work normally. Would the Gift not work on Vampires, force them to a healing rate as if they were human, or permanently keep them from healing the injury? Thanks for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1718-rurouni82","name":"rurouni82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T12:16:36-08:00","id":31824,"title":"","content":"If I were running a Vampire or crossover game, I'd rule it as &quot;can heal like normal for a vampire&quot;. If I were running a Werewolf game, I'd rule as &quot;vampires heal at normal human rate&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure the writer's intent was &quot;can heal like normal for a vampire&quot;, but various Blood Sorcery, Supernal Magics, etc are meant to <b>not </b>work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T15:43:42-08:00","id":31949,"title":"","content":"Vampires can only heal by spending Vitae, IIRC, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T16:47:32-08:00","id":31996,"title":"","content":"Yeah I like that part.<br /> Despite my love for Werewolf this has never come up in a game, and I'd probably make it so that the vampire afflicted had to actually seek medical attention and have the wound closed. Though I'd allow blood sorcery or other rites to do it, possibly some higher level disciplines, just not the unnatural vampire healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T08:31:30-08:00","id":32424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/31765-lingering-bite-on-the-undead?p=31949#post31949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can only heal by spending Vitae, IIRC, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, which is why &quot;healing like a normal person&quot; means they're SOL.<br /> <br /> I don't have the book in front of me, but it sounds like it's supposed to be a Gift that deals some damage and keeps bleeding until it heals at a slow, natural pace. Useful mostly for wounding (and maybe tracking) other Uratha, since they are known for healing quickly, and barring their usual methods of quick healing (spending Essence). When it comes to the supernatural community as a whole, it's a broad brush to paint with, but it would be most appropriate to just say that they can't heal <i>faster than normal</i> (for their species). When it comes to vampires, since they have no natural rate, they could spend BP to heal, but they couldn't use anything to downgrade it from lethal/agg to bashing/lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T01:17:24-08:00","id":34350,"title":"","content":"Per Blood and Smoke, Vitae-based healing happens unconsciously during the daysleep and needs to be actively suppressed if the vampire wants to save Vitae, so stopping them from instantly healing it while awake would seem to be the way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T10:18:57-08:00","id":35650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/31765-lingering-bite-on-the-undead?p=34350#post34350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per Blood and Smoke, Vitae-based healing happens unconsciously during the daysleep and needs to be actively suppressed if the vampire wants to save Vitae, so stopping them from instantly healing it while awake would seem to be the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems about right to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T23:03:39-08:00","id":43366,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the input. It hasn't come up yet, but I had a random Pure baddie that may or may not show up again for my vampires. I didn't want to cripple them permanently, just give them something to put them in touch with their mortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1718-rurouni82","name":"rurouni82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}